{:edb/db-before-t 1265 :edb/db-after-t 1266 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534578 50 #inst "2026-10-12T03:35:51.226Z" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059563 1071 "Find the inverse of ![](images/89/8967a472cff03599b1c2c94704fc9dc7272dc2a344d1876309dce1010a7ecc1f.svg)" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059563 1071 "Find the inverse of $[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 false] [17592186059563 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-12)+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n![](images/51/51ba8948d60b649bea88218e86b2ea39cbecfe8014367a3def09d2aeb7667460.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](images/b6/b6339df9152864283a9ed0b938c2183da94121edec8d5b434566b2953e5bd0b0.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{9}{2} & 7 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059563 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-12)+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}9 & -(-4) & -3 \\\\ -(14) & -8 & -(-4) \\\\ 3 & -(-2) & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{9}{2} & 7 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 false] [17592186059564 1071 "The entry $a'_{31}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n![](images/4b/4b816f3bc511cd6170658d9b75715fc6385feeea1e768cd44d1bd199b67bf853.svg) \nequals $1$. Find the value of $k$." 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059564 1071 "The entry $a'_{31}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ \nequals $1$. Find the value of $k$." 13194139534578 17592186045417 false] [17592186059565 1071 "Determine the entry $a'_{23}$ in the inverse of the matrix ![](images/96/967f00655054db75990de13f3634f8d0b320ffde849057ce8cc9a19c58754aa2.svg)" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059565 1071 "Determine the entry $a'_{23}$ in the inverse of the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 false] [17592186059754 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426309 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059755 1038 #edb/ref 17592186426308 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186059887 1050 1500.0 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186060933 1064 "We can calculate the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ using the following five-step algorithm.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant $\\det(A)$ of the matrix.\n\n**Step 2:** Form the **matrix $M$ of the minors** of $A,$ where each entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ is replaced by its minor $M_{ij}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} & {M}_{13} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22} & {M}_{23} \\\\ {M}_{31} & {M}_{32} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the **matrix $C$ of cofactors** by changing the sign of some entries of the matrix of the minors according to the **rule of alternating signs**:\n   \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}+ & - & + \\\\ - & + & - \\\\ + & - & +\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFor each entry of $M$, we change the sign if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$-$\". Otherwise, if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$+$\", then we don't change the entry.\n\nSo, the matrix of cofactors is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & -{M}_{12} & {M}_{13} \\\\ -{M}_{21} & {M}_{22} & -{M}_{23} \\\\ {M}_{31} & -{M}_{32} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors, $C^T.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & -{M}_{21} & {M}_{31} \\\\ -{M}_{12} & {M}_{22} & -{M}_{32} \\\\ {M}_{13} & -{M}_{23} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix:\n   \n\n$$\nA^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det ( A)}C^{T}\n$$\n\nIn other words, we divide each entry of the transpose of the matrix of cofactors by the determinant of the original matrix (which we computed in step 1).\n\nLet's see this in practice, in the next example." 13194139534578 17592186045417 false] [17592186060933 1064 "We can calculate the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ using the following five-step algorithm.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant $\\det(A)$ of the matrix.\n\n**Step 2:** Form the **matrix $M$ of the minors** of $A,$ where each entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ is replaced by its minor $M_{ij}\\mathbin{:}$\n   ![](images/14/14905267240a1e8eb7f54ae47b813c24aa5eb26415c419bbd0ec53425693309b.svg)\n\n**Step 3:** Create the **matrix $C$ of cofactors** by changing the sign of some entries of the matrix of the minors according to the **rule of alternating signs**:\n   \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}+ & - & + \\\\ - & + & - \\\\ + & - & +\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFor each entry of $M$, we change the sign if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$-$\". Otherwise, if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$+$\", then we don't change the entry.\n\nSo, the matrix of cofactors is given by\n\n![](images/a5/a57831b81711ce44dc46c2a3a91b18d8dbfe4078697805369097421351294d2e.svg)\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors, $C^T.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93df3291f387eaac0f6992b38e005f72b08b71b99c7cef8fe6a3b8f42662ebc.svg)\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix:\n   \n\n$$\nA^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det ( A)}C^{T}\n$$\n\nIn other words, we divide each entry of the transpose of the matrix of cofactors by the determinant of the original matrix (which we computed in step 1).\n\nLet's see this in practice, in the next example." 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426296 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426296 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426296 1083 #uuid "16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426297 1080 "1" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426297 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426297 1083 #uuid "332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426298 1080 "-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426298 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426298 1083 #uuid "39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426299 1080 "2" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426299 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426299 1083 #uuid "6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426300 1080 "-1" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426300 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426300 1083 #uuid "864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426301 1080 "-3[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426301 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426301 1083 #uuid "95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426302 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426302 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426302 1083 #uuid "b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426303 1080 "0" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426303 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426303 1083 #uuid "d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426304 1080 "-2" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426304 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426304 1083 #uuid "f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426305 1080 "-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426305 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426305 1083 #uuid "fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426296 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426298 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426301 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426302 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426305 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1077 "selection" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426298 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426306 1079 #uuid "4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426297 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426299 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426300 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426303 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426304 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1077 "selection" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426300 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426307 1079 #uuid "7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426307 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1069 "q-104435" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1071 "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $2.$ Find the value of $k.$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1072 #uuid "60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426308 1074 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-k-6)-0+1(6-k) \\\\  & =-k-6+6-k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-2-2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{k} & =2 \\\\ -2 & =2k \\\\ -\\frac{2}{2} & =k \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426306 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1069 "q-73478" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1071 "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-3.$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1072 #uuid "ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true] [17592186426309 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534578 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" 17592186426296 "answer-332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" 17592186426297 "answer-39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" 17592186426298 "answer-6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" 17592186426299 "answer-864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" 17592186426300 "answer-95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" 17592186426301 "answer-b9fbec83-d0b7-55ad-a7b0-15c8c1d2d21d" 17592186426302 "answer-d90a60bf-c9df-5642-a65f-043b1fbac549" 17592186426303 "answer-f712f3e2-029b-5a8a-b19e-340bb36a3186" 17592186426304 "answer-fc2f21f0-c001-5a27-883c-872065513e5c" 17592186426305 "answer-field-4b1f25d6-5390-5fe3-998f-b7a40d9649c3" 17592186426306 "answer-field-7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" 17592186426307 "question-60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" 17592186426308 "question-ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" 17592186426309} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
